# Proof, environment. Copy to .env.local for development, and set the same names
# in the Vercel dashboard for production. Nothing here is a secret except where
# it says so, and no secret belongs in git.

# --- Stripe -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every billing route is INERT without these: it returns 503 with the reason
# rather than half-working. Test-mode keys start sk_test_ and live sk_live_.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# From the webhook endpoint you create in the Stripe dashboard. Signature
# verification fails closed without it, so an unsigned request is never handled.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Price ids for the two monthly plans. NOT secrets, but they differ between test
# and live mode, and a plan with no price configured is unavailable rather than
# free. Create them as recurring monthly prices in the dashboard.
STRIPE_PRICE_KEPT_ONLINE=
STRIPE_PRICE_KEPT_SHARP=
# Which Stripe account this deployment is allowed to bill on, acct_... from the
# dashboard. Proof bills on its OWN account, separate from any other business, and
# this is the only check that can tell the two apart: a Stripe secret key does not
# encode which account it belongs to, so nothing else can. Optional, and STRONGLY
# recommended, because a wrong-account key does not fail. Checkout succeeds, the
# customer is charged, and the money lands in the other business's ledger.
STRIPE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# --- Licence signing ----------------------------------------------------------
# THE ONE REAL SECRET IN THIS FILE. The Ed25519 private half whose public half is
# compiled into licence/verify.mjs as k1. Whoever holds this can issue licences,
# so it lives in the Vercel dashboard and in a password manager, and nowhere else.
# Paste the whole PEM including the BEGIN and END lines.
PROOF_LICENCE_PRIVATE_KEY=
# Which key id to sign with. Must exist in ISSUER_PUBLIC_KEYS. Rotation: add the
# new public key there, deploy, then move this to the new id.
PROOF_LICENCE_KEY_ID=k1

# --- Email --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sending is INERT without both of these, and inert is reported rather than
# hidden: the apply form falls back to opening the visitor's own mail app, and an
# undelivered renewal licence is logged loudly because the customer has paid and
# cannot collect the token without being told.
# Needs a verified sending domain, which is why it is not on yet.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# The From address on a verified domain, e.g. hello@proofstudio.com
PROOF_MAIL_FROM=
# Where applications are delivered. Defaults to the founder's address.
PROOF_APPLY_TO=

# --- Site ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The canonical URL, used by the canonical link, og:image, JSON-LD, robots.txt
# and the sitemap. Change it HERE when a custom domain arrives and all five
# follow. Defaults to the Vercel production alias.
PROOF_SITE_URL=
